  "rule_for_models": "For a patient aged 65 or younger, report and cite a prescribed oral NSAID and an ACE inhibitor or ARB if they overlap on at least one day with no diuretic treatment evident on that day. Check every ingredient and use dates, directions, quantities and documented starts or stops, including earlier supplies that still cover the episode. Give no finding if the required courses do not overlap, the diuretic covers every common day, or the patient is outside the age range. If the pattern could qualify but age, indication or treatment dates are unclear, cite the relevant supplies, report a possible finding and ask only for the missing detail.",
  "cannot_be_seen": "Medicines obtained elsewhere or bought without a prescription are missing from this record. The supplies cannot show which doses the person took or how the medicines affected kidney function.",
  "ask_the_gp": "Could you review the need for the oral NSAID, check for supplies from other sources and review the latest kidney function?",
  "urgency": "routine",
  "draft": true,
